{"id": "EUVD-2026-86048", "enisaUuid": "ad88db36-5333-3696-94a6-30a6851b3b1c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: dsa: sja1105: flower: reject cross-chip redirect\n\ndsa_port_from_netdev() may return a valid port from a different switch\nchip. Programming another chip's port index into the local hardware\ncauses redirection to the wrong port, or an out-of-bounds access if the\nindex exceeds the local chip's port count.\n\nApply a minimal fix that adds a check to catch this case and adjusts the\nextack message. When cls->common.skip_sw is not set, the operation could\ninstead redirect to the upstream port and let the software or upstream\nswitch(es) handle the forward, but that is not addressed here.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T16:03:48", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-03T10:58:19", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6bf5158af52a5293e9160d8f2992c629ca14aa7d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/277f8611e017d3ff1ab06af58a6c538b55da1cc8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/eb177aa00c392de3dc530c34f173a962216f82dd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d0e54098c072b6064cdcf8039075ada8b88583da", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c999cc39775381b68ed66eae57c1425452672c0f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/abd7511e12b231798332afa04ed9bee9e84f9445", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cfa5274a5dc2a23b957da5dc806d2ac0c7a66af0"], "aliases": ["GHSA-fv9v-g8xq-3w88", "CVE-2026-97435"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1cea1b03-c669-3bab-a4b8-3fe47b6c6e16", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "1e0597cd-7d68-3f76-b90c-ab97c0c8f365", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "dfacc5a23e227cabdff41b6202f510398e90d36b <d0e54098c072b6064cdcf8039075ada8b88583da"}, {"id": "21fba953-7aa7-38f7-add8-f5006d4a9e8e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version":